# A dead straight line, for the one document that wants a ruler.
#
# Every other spline in this tree wanders on purpose: a track laid out straight
# reads as a ruled edge however ragged the material boundary on top of it is,
# because the eye finds the straightness at a scale above anything the
# transition solver works at.
#
# This one is straight for exactly that reason inverted. `wet_and_dry` is a
# comparison card, not a landscape — it lays six ground states out in parallel
# stripes so that two of them can be read against each other without either
# one's shape being part of the difference. A wandering axis would put the
# stripes at different widths in different parts of the plate, and every
# comparison across it would be confounded by how much of each state the eye
# happened to be looking at.
#
# It runs south-west to north-east so the stripes cross the isometric diamond
# corner to corner and every one of them reaches the camera at the same angle.

-40  -40
-20  -20
  0    0
 20   20
 40   40
